{"name":"Cabernet","hex":"#8e5b68","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabernet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Cabernet Sauvignon, a wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabernet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cabernet Sauvignon","blocks":[{"text":"Cabernet Sauvignon is one of the world's most widely recognized red wine grape varieties. It is grown in nearly every major wine producing country among a diverse spectrum of climates from Australia and British Columbia, Canada to Lebanon's Beqaa Valley."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Red_Mountain_Cabernet_Sauvignon_grapes_from_Hedge_Vineyards.jpg/330px-Red_Mountain_Cabernet_Sauvignon_grapes_from_Hedge_Vineyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabernet_Sauvignon","wikidata":"Q207310"},{"title":"Cabernet Franc","blocks":[{"text":"Cabernet Franc is one of the major black grape varieties worldwide. It is principally grown for blending with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot in the Bordeaux style, but can also be vinified alone, as in the Loire's Chinon. In addition to being used in blends and produced as a varietal in Canada, Lake Erie AVA in Pennsylvania, and across the United States and Argentina, it is sometimes made into ice wine in those regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Cabernet-franc.jpg/330px-Cabernet-franc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabernet_Franc","wikidata":"Q63591"},{"title":"Cabernet (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Cabernet is a 2025 narrative role-playing video game developed by Party for Introverts, and published by Akupara Games. It was released for Microsoft Windows, Nintendo Switch, PlayStation 4, PlayStation 5, and Xbox Series S|X on February 20, 2025. The game is about vampires."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/92/Cabernet_KeyArt.png/330px-Cabernet_KeyArt.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabernet_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q130326056"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Cabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg/500px-Cabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Cabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg/1280px-Cabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Cabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg/500px-Cabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cabernet Franc","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACabernet_Franc_Weinsberg_20060909.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Sauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg/500px-Sauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Sauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg/1280px-Sauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Sauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg/500px-Sauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sauvignon blanc","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASauvignon_blanc_vlasotince_vineyards.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Cab_sauvignon_leaf.JPG/500px-Cab_sauvignon_leaf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Cab_sauvignon_leaf.JPG/500px-Cab_sauvignon_leaf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cabernet Sauvignon leaf. In cooler climate conditions, vines will focus more energy in producing foliage, which is needed to capture sunlight for photosynthesis, rather than ripening grapes. This makes canopy management and aggressive pruning an important consideration for growers.[13]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACab_sauvignon_leaf.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Original_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg/500px-Original_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Original_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg/1280px-Original_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Original_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg/500px-Original_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cabernet Sauvignon in Washington State, planted in 1973 at Red Willow Vineyard in the Yakima Valley.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOriginal_1973_Cabernet_Sauvignon_from_Red_Willow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mthomebrew_maceration.JPG/500px-Mthomebrew_maceration.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mthomebrew_maceration.JPG/500px-Mthomebrew_maceration.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"During the maceration period, color, flavor and tannins are extracted from the skins. The addition of stems and seeds will increase the tannic content of the wine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMthomebrew_maceration.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Large_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg/500px-Large_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Large_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg/1280px-Large_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Large_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg/500px-Large_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Large oak barrels, like these used in Tuscany bring less wine into contact with the wood and therefore leave the resulting wine with less oak influence.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarge_botti_size_oak_barrels_in_Chianti.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Ch%C3%A2teau_d%27Armailhacq_53_detail.JPG/330px-Ch%C3%A2teau_d%27Armailhacq_53_detail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Ch%C3%A2teau_d%27Armailhacq_53_detail.JPG/330px-Ch%C3%A2teau_d%27Armailhacq_53_detail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Armand d'Armailhac of Château d'Armailhac (bottle picture) and Baron Hector de Brane of Château Mouton were important figures in the establishment of Cabernet Sauvignon in Bordeaux.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACh%C3%A2teau_d'Armailhacq_53_detail.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Montalcino_002.jpg/500px-Montalcino_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb